# Unique parabolic extension of a character across -1

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.Period.existsUnique_isParabolicHom_sup_zpowers_neg_one_apply_eq`
(`c2d4705b-da14-5756-838c-dc8765afc682`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `2c3bf78f-e9c1-5ebb-8b95-4b6bac3b5e01`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, let $A$ be an additive abelian group, and
let $\psi$ be an additive homomorphism from $\Gamma$, regarded as an additive group via `Additive`,
to $A$ (equivalently, a homomorphism of groups $\Gamma \to A$). Assume $\psi$ is parabolic in the
sense of the predicate [`ModularCurve.Period.IsParabolicHom`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L15):
for every $\gamma \in \Gamma$ whose underlying integer matrix satisfies $(\operatorname{tr}\gamma)^2
= 4$, one has $\psi(\gamma) = 0$. Write $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$ for the subgroup of
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma$ together with the integer powers of $-1$. The
assertion is that there is exactly one additive homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\Gamma \sqcup \langle
-1 \rangle$ (again viewed additively) to $A$ with the two properties: $\varphi$ is parabolic, i.e.
$\varphi(\delta) = 0$ for every $\delta$ in $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$ with
$(\operatorname{tr}\delta)^2 = 4$; and $\varphi$ restricts to $\psi$ along the inclusion, i.e.
$\varphi(\gamma) = \psi(\gamma)$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma$, where on the left $\gamma$ is viewed
as an element of the larger subgroup.

This says that parabolic characters do not see the centre: restriction along $\Gamma \hookrightarrow
\pm\Gamma$ is a bijection between the parabolic characters of $\pm\Gamma$ and those of $\Gamma$,
which permits period computations to be carried out on the subgroup generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$.
It is used in the comparison of cup pairings under conjugation
([`ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair_comp_eq_of_conjRel`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.CupPairing.pair_comp_eq_of_conjRel))
and in the rank formula
[`ModularCurve.six_mul_level_mul_finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_add_eq`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.six_mul_level_mul_finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_add_eq).

